ich analyzes more than 100  samples per day well again that also  depends on the analysis task yeah mm it  is tasks for example for for a soil  analysis is only the screening on of the  soil for metals and heavy metal  concentration then for example a  handheld instrument will do then also a  portable instrument will do and also the  spectral Depot's will do an outstanding  job although it must be mentioned if you  really want to go down too low detection  limits then typically in a lab that runs  100 samples or more per day then ICP  instruments are used but you also have  to keep in my  always that you also then have to manage  the sample preparation for that high  amount of samples okay thank you  Olaf does air cooling reply require any  extraction to outside the lab well let's  say it's recommended because it is it's  obviously warm air and this is very much  the same as using a external cooling  system which is placed in the lab also  that dissipates heat into the lab and  that's also something which is not quite  desired because it heats up the room so  you also want to you know place it  outside the laboratory and the same  applies where this air which comes out  of the instrument it is it is warm and  so it's obviously best if you extract it  to the outside however if the room is  large enough or you have an air  condition and you are able to to keep  the temperature in the laboratory  relatively constant you know round about  20-25 Celsius then this is also not a  problem to do because what comes out of  the generator is really nothing but warm  air obviously I mean the front part the  plasma requires an extraction because  the plasma gases they need to be  extracted to the outside thank you  Dirk  the analysis results using ICP and XRF  always comparable where are the  differences or impact on the results not  always comparable if you for example  look at some of the certificates that  are available for reference samples then  you in some cases will find d